# configuration file for the three stage flame test (with noise metrics)

REQUIRES Driver
REQUIRES physics/Hydro
REQUIRES physics/sourceTerms/Flame/FlameEffects/BurnParametric

IF withParticles
   PARTICLETYPE passive INITMETHOD lattice MAPMETHOD weighted ADVMETHOD rungekutta
   REQUIRES Particles/ParticlesMain
   REQUIRES Particles/ParticlesInitialization/Lattice
   REQUIRES Particles/ParticlesMapping/meshWeighting/CIC
   REQUESTS IO/IOMain/
   REQUESTS IO/IOParticles
ENDIF

# override defaults
PARAMETER useBurn      BOOLEAN true

D rho_ambient Density of unburned material
D t_ambient   Temperature of unburned material
PARAMETER rho_ambient  REAL    2.e9
PARAMETER t_ambient    REAL    5.0e7

D ignite Determines if simulation begins with a flame front in it
D frac_perturb Size of burned region, scaled to domain size (generally x extent)
PARAMETER ignite       BOOLEAN FALSE
PARAMETER frac_perturb REAL    .5

D pseudo_1d If true a planar flame front is created, otherwise a spherical one is
D & planar configuration is as follows based on other parameters
D &         y ^          .
D &           |    \     .
D &           |     \    .
D &           |      \ t .
D &      yctr +       +  .  fuel
D &           |        \ .   
D &           | ash     \
D &           |          \
D &           +-------+--------------------------> x
D &                   |
D &               frac_ptrb * x extent
D xctr_perturb Planar: unused
D &            Spherical: x coordinate of center of spherical burned region
D yctr_perturb Planar: pivot point of planar interface (see diagram with pseudo_1d)
D &            Spherical: y coordinate of center of spherical burned region
D zctr_perturb Planar: unused
D &            Spherical: z coordinate of center of spherical burned region
D theta angle between surface normal to planar flame surface and x axis (see diagram with pseudo_1d)

PARAMETER pseudo_1d    BOOLEAN FALSE
PARAMETER xctr_perturb REAL    1.e-4
PARAMETER yctr_perturb REAL    1.e-4
PARAMETER zctr_perturb REAL    1.e-4
PARAMETER theta        REAL    0.

D c_frac Initial fraction of carbon in unburned material
D ne_frac Initial fraction of ne22 in unburned material
PARAMETER c_frac       REAL    0.5
PARAMETER ne_frac      REAL    0.0

# if this variable is present, flame speed unit will save the local
# calculated flame speed to it
VARIABLE fspd


PARTICLEPROP    dens            REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO dens         FROM VARIABLE dens
PARTICLEPROP    temp            REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO temp         FROM VARIABLE temp
PARTICLEPROP    pres            REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO pres         FROM VARIABLE pres
PARTICLEPROP    flam            REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO flam         FROM MASS_SCALAR FLAM
PARTICLEPROP    phfa            REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO phfa         FROM MASS_SCALAR phfa
PARTICLEPROP    phaq            REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO phaq         FROM MASS_SCALAR phaq
PARTICLEPROP    phqn            REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO phqn         FROM MASS_SCALAR phqn
PARTICLEPROP    ye              REAL
PARTICLEMAP     TO ye           FROM MASS_SCALAR ye

